"ulāika","verse_key":"2:177"},{"pos":47,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"(are) the ones who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"2:177"},{"pos":48,"ar":"صَدَقُوا۟ ۖ","en_gloss":"are true","transliteration":"ṣadaqū","verse_key":"2:177"},{"pos":49,"ar":"وَأُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ","en_gloss":"and those","transliteration":"wa-ulāika","verse_key":"2:177"},{"pos":50,"ar":"هُمُ","en_gloss":"[they]","transliteration":"humu","verse_key":"2:177"},{"pos":51,"ar":"ٱلْمُتَّقُونَ","en_gloss":"(are) the righteous","transliteration":"l-mutaqūna","verse_key":"2:177"},{"pos":52,"ar":"١٧٧","en_gloss":"(177)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:177"}]},{"verse_key":"2:178","surah":2,"ayah":178,"ar_uthmani":"يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْقِصَاصُ فِى ٱلْقَتْلَى ۖ ٱلْحُرُّ بِٱلْحُرِّ وَٱلْعَبْدُ بِٱلْعَبْدِ وَٱلْأُنثَىٰ بِٱلْأُنثَىٰ ۚ فَمَنْ عُفِىَ لَهُۥ مِنْ أَخِيهِ شَىْءٌ فَٱتِّبَاعٌۢ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ وَأَدَآءٌ إِلَيْهِ بِإِحْسَـٰنٍ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ تَخْفِيفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ ۗ فَمَنِ ٱعْتَدَىٰ بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ فَلَهُۥ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"You who believe, fair retribution is prescribed for you in cases of murder: the free man for the free man, the slave for the slave, the female for the female. But if the culprit is pardoned by his aggrieved brother, this shall be adhered to fairly, and the culprit shall pay what is due in a good way. This is an alleviation from your Lord and an act of mercy. If anyone then exceeds these limits, grievous suffering awaits him.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا","en_gloss":"O you","transliteration":"yāayyuhā","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ءَامَنُوا۟","en_gloss":"believe[d]","transliteration":"āmanū","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":4,"ar":"كُتِبَ","en_gloss":"Prescribed","transliteration":"kutiba","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":5,"ar":"عَلَيْكُمُ","en_gloss":"for you","transliteration":"ʿalaykumu","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلْقِصَاصُ","en_gloss":"(is) the legal retribution","transliteration":"l-qiṣāṣu","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":7,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ٱلْقَتْلَى ۖ","en_gloss":"(the matter of) the murdered","transliteration":"l-qatlā","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":9,"ar":"ٱلْحُرُّ","en_gloss":"the freeman","transliteration":"l-ḥuru","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":10,"ar":"بِٱلْحُرِّ","en_gloss":"for the freeman","transliteration":"bil-ḥuri","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":11,"ar":"وَٱلْعَبْدُ","en_gloss":"and the slave","transliteration":"wal-ʿabdu","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":12,"ar":"بِٱلْعَبْدِ","en_gloss":"for the slave","transliteration":"bil-ʿabdi","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":13,"ar":"وَٱلْأُنثَىٰ","en_gloss":"and the female","transliteration":"wal-unthā","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":14,"ar":"بِٱلْأُنثَىٰ ۚ","en_gloss":"for the female","transliteration":"bil-unthā","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":15,"ar":"فَمَنْ","en_gloss":"But whoever","transliteration":"faman","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":16,"ar":"عُفِىَ","en_gloss":"is pardoned","transliteration":"ʿufiya","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":17,"ar":"لَهُۥ","en_gloss":"[for it]","transliteration":"lahu","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":18,"ar":"مِنْ","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":19,"ar":"أَخِيهِ","en_gloss":"his brother","transliteration":"akhīhi","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":20,"ar":"شَىْءٌۭ","en_gloss":"anything","transliteration":"shayon","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":21,"ar":"فَٱتِّبَاعٌۢ","en_gloss":"then follows up","transliteration":"fa-ittibāʿun","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":22,"ar":"بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ","en_gloss":"with suitable","transliteration":"bil-maʿrūfi","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":23,"ar":"وَأَدَآءٌ","en_gloss":"[and] payment","transliteration":"wa-adāon","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":24,"ar":"إِلَيْهِ","en_gloss":"to him","transliteration":"ilayhi","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":25,"ar":"بِإِحْسَـٰنٍۢ ۗ","en_gloss":"with kindness","transliteration":"bi-iḥ'sānin","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":26,"ar":"ذَٰلِكَ","en_gloss":"That (is)","transliteration":"dhālika","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":27,"ar":"تَخْفِيفٌۭ","en_gloss":"a concession","transliteration":"takhfīfun","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":28,"ar":"مِّن","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":29,"ar":"رَّبِّكُمْ","en_gloss":"your Lord","transliteration":"rabbikum","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":30,"ar":"وَرَحْمَةٌۭ ۗ","en_gloss":"and mercy","transliteration":"waraḥmatun","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":31,"ar":"فَمَنِ","en_gloss":"Then whoever","transliteration":"famani","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":32,"ar":"ٱعْتَدَىٰ","en_gloss":"transgresses","transliteration":"iʿ'tadā","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":33,"ar":"بَعْدَ","en_gloss":"after","transliteration":"baʿda","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":34,"ar":"ذَٰلِكَ","en_gloss":"that","transliteration":"dhālika","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":35,"ar":"فَلَهُۥ","en_gloss":"then for him","transliteration":"falahu","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":36,"ar":"عَذَابٌ","en_gloss":"(is) a punishment","transliteration":"ʿadhābun","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":37,"ar":"أَلِيمٌۭ","en_gloss":"painful","transliteration":"alīmun","verse_key":"2:178"},{"pos":38,"ar":"١٧٨","en_gloss":"(178)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:178"}]},{"verse_key":"2:179","surah":2,"ayah":179,"ar_uthmani":"وَلَكُمْ فِى ٱلْقِصَاصِ حَيَوٰةٌ يَـٰٓأُو۟لِى ٱلْأَلْبَـٰبِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Fair retribution saves life for you, people of understanding, so that you may guard yourselves against what is wrong. When death approaches one of you who leaves wealth,","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَلَكُمْ","en_gloss":"And for you","transliteration":"walakum","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":2,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلْقِصَاصِ","en_gloss":"the legal retribution","transliteration":"l-qiṣāṣi","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":4,"ar":"حَيَوٰةٌۭ","en_gloss":"(is) life","transliteration":"ḥayatun","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":5,"ar":"يَـٰٓأُو۟لِى","en_gloss":"O men","transliteration":"yāulī","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلْأَلْبَـٰبِ","en_gloss":"(of) understanding","transliteration":"l-albābi","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لَعَلَّكُمْ","en_gloss":"So that you may","transliteration":"laʿallakum","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":8,"ar":"تَتَّقُونَ","en_gloss":"(become) righteous","transliteration":"tattaqūna","verse_key":"2:179"},{"pos":9,"ar":"١٧٩","en_gloss":"(179)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:179"}]},{"verse_key":"2:180","surah":2,"ayah":180,"ar_uthmani":"كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذَا حَضَرَ أَحَدَكُمُ ٱلْمَوْتُ إِن تَرَكَ خَيْرًا ٱلْوَصِيَّةُ لِلْوَٰلِدَيْنِ وَٱلْأَقْرَبِينَ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ ۖ حَقًّا عَلَى ٱلْمُتَّقِينَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"it is prescribed that he should make a proper bequest to parents and close relatives- a duty incumbent on those who are mindful of God.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"كُتِبَ","en_gloss":"Prescribed","transliteration":"kutiba","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":2,"ar":"عَلَيْكُمْ","en_gloss":"for you","transliteration":"ʿalaykum","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":3,"ar":"إِذَا","en_gloss":"when","transliteration":"idhā","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":4,"ar":"حَضَرَ","en_gloss":"approaches","transliteration":"ḥaḍara","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":5,"ar":"أَحَدَكُمُ","en_gloss":"any of you","transliteration":"aḥadakumu","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلْمَوْتُ","en_gloss":"[the] death","transliteration":"l-mawtu","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":7,"ar":"إِن","en_gloss":"if","transliteration":"in","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":8,"ar":"تَرَكَ","en_gloss":"he leaves","transliteration":"taraka","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":9,"ar":"خَيْرًا","en_gloss":"good","transliteration":"khayran","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":10,"ar":"ٱلْوَصِيَّةُ","en_gloss":"(making) the will","transliteration":"l-waṣiyatu","verse_key":"2:180"},{"pos":11,"ar":"لِلْوَٰلِدَيْنِ","en_gloss":"for the parents","transliteration":"lil'wāl